# Memphis and Tulsa plan

diagram reroute dir=LR title="Reroute from 2026-11-23"
reroute: memphis "Memphis" svc "104.0% now, 100.0% after" focus
reroute: tulsa "Tulsa" svc "94.3% now, 99.5% after" focus
reroute: omaha "Omaha" svc "up to 7,200 spare"
reroute: memphis -> tulsa : 2,200 a day
reroute: memphis --> omaha : adds a day

From 2026-11-23, 2,200 Memphis parcels a day move to Tulsa. Memphis lands at exactly 100.0% and Tulsa at 99.5%. Both would be at their limit with no slack.

Omaha could take up to 7,200 more parcels a day, but rerouting there adds a day of transit.

step Reroute 2,200 Memphis parcels a day to Tulsa | 2026-11-23
step All 640 seasonal workers start (210 for Memphis) | by 2026-11-16

# Risks

!! Any outage or weather delay at Memphis or Tulsa during the window has nowhere to go except Omaha, which adds a day of transit.

!! The plan relies on all 640 seasonal workers starting by 2026-11-16. A late start leaves Memphis and Tulsa short with no headroom to absorb it.
